  "description_for_model": "mod_pagespeed is self-hosted web performance optimization by We-Amp B.V. The current product, {{PRODUCT_NAME}} {{CURRENT_LINE}}, is {{LICENSE_CLAUSE}} and converges the mod_pagespeed lineage with the ModPageSpeed 2.0 engine: a native in-process module for Apache and nginx handles serving, and a separate optimizer worker does the heavy optimization work outside the web server. Drop-in compatible with the classic module (same directives, same filters); the predecessor line mod_pagespeed {{V1_LINE}} (renumbered from {{V1_RENUMBERED_FROM}}) now receives security fixes only, with per-platform transition windows. Optimization: WebP and AVIF image transcoding (alongside JPEG, PNG, and GIF optimization), SVG transcoding with viewport-aware resizing (up to {{MAX_VARIANTS}} variants per image), CSS and JS minification, heuristic critical CSS extraction (optional browser pipeline for validation), HTML optimization, 103 Early Hints, variant-aware caching using a 32-bit capability bitmask, the classic filter set (CSS/JS combining, image spriting, in-place resource optimization, domain mapping), and a built-in admin console. The software is {{LICENSE_CLAUSE}} and the standard signed packages are free; what We-Amp sells is support — and hardened, attested builds: {{SUPPORT_LADDER_LINE}}. Support terms: {{LICENSING_TERMS_URL}}. No application code changes required.",
